WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.035 --> 00:00:03.529
Goal: prepare a website handoff
the next owner can execute.

2
00:00:03.576 --> 00:00:08.022
Before any model runs, Organizational
AI Memory selects an approved prompt,

3
00:00:08.057 --> 00:00:11.575
workflow, and source-first
decision, each with review state,

4
00:00:11.622 --> 00:00:14.222
why-it-worked context, and source lineage.

5
00:00:14.246 --> 00:00:18.576
In this fresh capture, Spark creates
six cited steps from those records.

6
00:00:18.692 --> 00:00:22.500
Each step keeps its selected
asset and source-turn citations.

7
00:00:22.616 --> 00:00:25.031
Deterministic selection
remains authoritative.

8
00:00:25.112 --> 00:00:28.456
Personal memory stays owner-only
until revision consent.

9
00:00:28.502 --> 00:00:32.101
A locked Linux agent retrieves it only
through a broker with revision and

10
00:00:32.218 --> 00:00:34.632
SHA-256 citation.

11
00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:39.509
Seven runtime checks deny source,
model credentials, direct PostgreSQL,

12
00:00:39.532 --> 00:00:43.503
and outbound sockets. Editing
resets access until re-consent.

13
00:00:43.619 --> 00:00:46.881
Spark adapts the plan; it
cannot decide company truth.

14
00:00:46.997 --> 00:00:50.550
When people move on, the organization
keeps reviewed capability,

15
00:00:50.619 --> 00:00:51.757
not private memory.
